<h1>PRACTICUM REPORT</h1>
<p class="center"><b>Project Title:</b> TravelNest - Multi-Vendor Travel Booking System</p>
<p class="center"><b>Project Type:</b> Web Application (Laravel/PHP)</p>
<p class="center"><b>Student ID:</b> 21303158</p>
<p class="center"><b>Department:</b> Computer Science and Engineering</p>
<p class="center"><b>Date:</b> April 2026</p>

<div class="page-break"></div>

<h2>Abstract</h2>
<p>
This practicum work presents the design and implementation of TravelNest, a Laravel-based multi-vendor travel booking system. The system supports end-to-end customer booking and payment workflows, including package discovery, booking creation, coupon application, secure payment processing, and booking confirmation. In addition to customer-facing functions, the platform provides a comprehensive administrative panel for managing agencies, users, packages, bookings, hotels, transport data, notifications, reports, and platform settings.
</p>
<p>
The project follows the MVC architectural pattern and uses a relational database schema with migration-driven evolution. Payment integration is implemented through a gateway callback architecture (success, fail, cancel, IPN), and role-based access control is applied to secure administration features. The resulting application demonstrates practical full-stack development skills including data modeling, backend validation, business logic implementation, route protection, and operational reporting.
</p>

